WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.852
2,138 registered lobbying contacts.

00:00:04.802 --> 00:00:07.131
One organization.

00:00:07.131 --> 00:00:11.039
A direct legislative pipeline from lobbying to law.

00:00:11.039 --> 00:00:19.631
The Centre for Israel and Jewish Affairs — CIJA — is one of the most active lobbying organizations in Canada's federal registry.

00:00:19.631 --> 00:00:26.407
Their lobbying contacts span the Prime Minister's Office, the Justice Department, and key committee members.

00:00:26.407 --> 00:00:37.092
The documented pipeline follows a clear sequence: IHRA definition adoption, Criminal Code amendments, Human Rights Act civil remedies, and MAID expansion.

00:00:37.092 --> 00:00:39.881
Each stage built on the last.

00:00:39.881 --> 00:00:48.210
Every data point in this analysis comes from Canada's own lobbying registry, Hansard records, and published committee testimony.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:53.578
These are not allegations — they are the government's own documented contacts.
